                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Appendix 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Article XVI of the consular convention between the
                        United States and Austria-Hungary, concluded July 11, 1810</hi>.</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article XVI</hi>.</p>
                <p>In case of the death of a citizen of the United States in the Austrian-Hungarian
                    Monarchy, or of a citizen of the Austrian-Hungarian Monarchy in the United
                    States, without having any known heirs or testamentary executors by him
                    appointed, the competent local authorities shall inform the consuls or consular
                    agents of the State to which the deceased belonged, of the circumstances, in
                    order that the necessary information may be immediately forwarded to the parties
                    interested.</p>
            </div>
